    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math>&nbsp;is a light rigid rod, which is rotating about a vertical axis passing through end&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> . A spring of force constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;and natural length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> &nbsp;is attached at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and its other end is attached to a small bead of mass&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>. The bead can slide without friction on the rod. At the initial moment, the bead is at rest (w.r.t the rod) and the spring is unstretched. Select incorrect options&nbsp;:</p>\r\r\r <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0032416_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 212px; height: 151px;\" /></p>\r",
